ented endocrine abnormalities or skin involvement (features favoring lymphoid neoplasm) in the vignette contradict lymphoid neoplasm (B2) as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Absence of lymphoid-specific features weakly argues against lymphoid neoplasm."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 35% blasts in peripheral blood contradict lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorder (B4) in favor of myeloid or lymphoid neoplasms (B1/B2)?", "summary": "High blast count is atypical for plasma cell disorders, strongly supporting myeloid/lymphoid neoplasms."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B2", 0.36], ["B1", 0.32], ["B4", 0.2]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.46], ["B4", 0.447], ["B1.1", 0.276]]}, {"top": [["B4", 0.418], ["B1", 0.31], ["B2", 0.242]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading hypothesis (B4) posterior 0.418 < 0.75. Dangerous alternatives (B1: 0.31, danger 0.8) remain unresolved with actionable differences between subtypes (AML vs CML-BC vs MDS-EB). Depth limit (3) reached but posterior threshold unmet."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.35, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.4177413928451273, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Vitamin B12 deficiency', 'Abnormal vitamin B12 level', 'elevated white blood cell count', 'Lymphocytosis', 'B-cell lymphoma', 'elevated red blood cell count'}", "mode_policy":